From 3d7c3bcb198ea2d86af5dbd73ac60b3ec6088ae7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nvidia-prolapse <nvidia-prolapse@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:30:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] util/disk_cache: add disk_cache_create_with_path()

Drivers have no way to place a disk cache in a directory of their choosing:
disk_cache_create() derives the location from MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR,
XDG_CACHE_HOME or HOME, all process-global, and disk_cache_create_custom()
only names a subdirectory of that location, always uses the database
backend and drops driver_flags from the keys.

Some platforms give each application a private directory that none of those
can name. On Android that is the application's code cache, a sibling of
TMPDIR (Context.getCodeCacheDir()); the global mesa.shader.cache.dir
property cannot point every application at its own one.

disk_cache_create_with_path() creates the cache at an absolute path given by
the caller (creating the last component if needed), with the type and size
limit chosen by the usual options and driver_flags in every key. Choosing a
path is the opt-in, so the cache is enabled on every platform unless
MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE is set; Android's disabled-by-default only
applies to the default location. The type/size selection of
disk_cache_create() moves into a helper shared by both.
